@startuml
title Vapor Client, Platform, and App Runtime Model

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Vapor Platform Server" {
    component "Identity" as Identity
    component "Registry" as Registry
    component "Diagnostics" as Diagnostics
    component "Docs" as Docs
    component "Future Matchmaking /\nSession Directory" as Match
}

package "Vapor Client" {
    component "Launcher / SDK / CLI" as ClientSurface
    component "Platform Client" as ClientPlatform
    component "App Client Runtime" as AppClient
}

package "Vapor App Server" {
    component "Platform Client" as ServerPlatform
    component "App Server Runtime" as AppServer
}

ClientSurface --> ClientPlatform
ClientSurface --> AppClient

ClientPlatform --> Identity : Platform communication
ClientPlatform --> Registry : Platform communication
ClientPlatform --> Diagnostics : Platform communication
ClientPlatform --> Match : Platform communication

ServerPlatform --> Identity : Platform communication
ServerPlatform --> Registry : Platform communication
ServerPlatform --> Match : register / authorize

AppClient <==> AppServer : App-session communication

note bottom of AppClient
Effective Engine/Game defines
App-specific runtime networking semantics.
end note

note bottom of AppServer
Vapor hosts/orchestrates the runtime;
it does not mandate one universal
replication or simulation protocol.
end note

note right of Match
Platform services may help establish
a session without becoming the
App-session data path.
end note

@enduml